INSIGHT code licensing scope
============================

The MIT License below applies to original INSIGHT software code: Python source
in backend/, Rust source in crates/insight-core/, TypeScript/JavaScript/CSS/HTML
source in frontend/, and project-authored build, configuration, and automation
code. It also applies to project-authored test code, but not to excluded data
that test code reads or embeds. Paths in this notice are repository-relative.

This is a code-only grant, not a license for every file in this repository.
The following are excluded from this grant:

- Research and reference data, source-derived tables, transcriptions, study
  metadata and research outputs, wherever stored or embedded. In particular:
  backend/reference_data/**, backend/fii_foods.csv,
  backend/validation/reference_result_v1_goldens.json, and
  crates/insight-core/fixtures/**. Dataset/fixture exclusions are conservative
  and do not assert that every excluded value is subject to copyright.
- docs/** and reports/**, including research prose, evidence, screenshots,
  and copies or extracts of published material.
- Images, icons, fonts, animations, branding and other non-code assets,
  including frontend/assets/**, frontend/icons/**, frontend/public/**,
  and image/font assets in frontend/android/**.
- Third-party code, dependencies, generated third-party components and other
  material with its own copyright or license notices. Those notices and
  applicable upstream terms remain in effect. In particular,
  frontend/android/gradlew and frontend/android/gradlew.bat retain Apache-2.0
  terms; no rights in Gradle or other dependencies are granted by this notice.

No new permission for excluded material is granted here. This notice does not
claim ownership of third-party material, override rights supplied by its owners
or applicable law, or certify research-data redistribution rights. Those rights
must be checked separately. Copying or embedding excluded data into a binary,
fixture, or another file does not bring it within the MIT grant. Keep this scope
notice with the MIT License when redistributing covered code.

